=== narrow ===

 show me how to count the go files


A loop over the listing is the shortest
way to say it.

Try this.

for NAME in $(ls *.go); do echo "$NAME
is quite a long line indeed"; done

That is all.

And a table, which changes shape as its
rows arrive:

┌──────┬───────────────────────────────┐
│ Tool │ What it does when it is asked │
│      │ to                            │
├──────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ read │ takes a file and hands it     │
│      │ back to you                   │
├──────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ grep │ walks the whole tree looking  │
│      │ for a pattern                 │
└──────┴───────────────────────────────┘

That is the lot.

And a nested list, whose markers arrive
before the items they introduce:

• read takes a file and hands it back
  • and says how big it was
  • and leaves it where it found it
• grep walks the tree for a pattern

That is the lot.
